                <pb facs="0458" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg364"/>

                <head>No. 268.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Roustan to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the French Republic in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 14, 1887</date>. (Received April
                    14.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor
                    herewith to transmit to you a copy of a dispatch, with in closures, which has
                    just been addressed to me by my Government in relation to the convention for the
                    protection, of submarine cables.</p>
                <p>I should be very grateful to you if you could enable me, at no distant date, to
                    reply to the inquiry of the minister of foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. Roustan.</hi></signed></closer>




